# Package Management

- Always use `pnpm` instead of `yarn`, `npm`, or `npx`
- Use workspace protocol (`workspace:*`) for internal package dependencies
- Run commands from the root when possible, using `pnpm run --filter` for workspace-specific commands

```bash
# ❌ BAD
npm install lodash
yarn add lodash
npx tsc

# ✅ GOOD
pnpm add lodash
pnpm run --filter @light-git/backend build
pnpm run --filter @light-git/frontend test
```

## Build Commands (from repo root)

```bash
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm run build                          # Build all packages
pnpm run --filter @light-git/backend build
pnpm run --filter @light-git/frontend build
pnpm run --filter @light-git/core build
pnpm run --filter @light-git/shared build
```

## Test Commands (from repo root)

```bash
pnpm run --filter @light-git/frontend test          # Vitest (frontend)
pnpm run --filter @light-git/frontend test:watch    # Vitest watch mode
pnpm run test-node                                    # Jasmine (backend, via root script)
```

## Adding Dependencies

```bash
# Add to a specific package
pnpm --filter @light-git/backend add some-package

# Add workspace dependency
pnpm --filter @light-git/frontend add @light-git/shared@workspace:*
```
